    {
      "id": "s09",
      "file": "synthetic/s09.wav",
      "tags": [
        "medium",
        "fillers",
        "synthetic"
      ],
      "status": "ok",
      "stt_ms": 10401,
      "audio_seconds": 13.87225,
      "stt_text": "So, you m? Two unrelated things. The onboarding screen feels too long, I think we should cut it down to, like, three steps. And separately, I keep forgetting to stretch in the evenings which is basically why my back hurts.",
      "wer": 0.05128205128205128,
      "llm_total_ms": 11692,
      "llm_ttft_ms": 7117,
      "llm_chunks": 40,
      "llm_timed_out": false,
      "llm_fallback": false,
      "folder": "Ideas",
      "expected_folder": null,
      "corrected_text": "Onboarding screen feels too long, should cut it down to three steps. I keep forgetting to stretch in evenings, back hurts.",
      "content_recall": 0.5641025641025641,
      "fillers_remaining": 0,
      "missing_facts": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "file": "synthetic/s11.wav",
      "tags": [
        "long",
        "synthetic"
      ],
      "status": "ok",
      "stt_ms": 5043,
      "audio_seconds": 39.4755625,
      "stt_text": "I've been thinking about how I capture ideas during the day and the problem is not that I don't have ideas. The problem is that by the time I get my phone out, unlock it, find the right app and start typing. The thoughts has already changed. What I remember is a summary of the idea not the idea itself. So the whole point of this app is to remove every step between having a thought and saving it. I press two buttons I talk and I'm done. Everything else, the transcription, the cleanup, the sorting into folders can happen later, when I'm not pay attention. If that works reliably I think I will actually trust it and trust is what makes a tool part of your day.",
      "wer": 0.023255813953488372,
      "llm_total_ms": 25878,
      "llm_ttft_ms": 6912,
      "llm_chunks": 167,
