      "llm_fallback": false,
      "folder": "Ideas",
      "expected_folder": null,
      "corrected_text": "I've been thinking about how I capture ideas during the day. The problem is not that I don't have ideas. The problem is that by the time I get my phone out, unlock it, find the right app, and start typing, the thoughts have already changed. What I remember is a summary of the idea, not the idea itself. So the whole point of this app is to remove every step between having a thought and saving it. I press two buttons, I talk, and I'm done. Everything else, the transcription, the cleanup, the sorting into folders, can happen later, when I'm not paying attention. If that works reliably, I think I will actually trust it, and trust is what makes a tool part of your day.",
