      "stt_ms": 10950,
      "audio_seconds": 75.93525,
      "stt_text": "Here is a longer note about the plan for next few weeks, so I don't lose track of it. The first priority is reliability. If I press the buttons and nothing is recorded. Even once I will stop trusting the app. So capture has to work every single time, with the screen off in my pocket and when the app has been closed for hours. The second priority is the quality of the text. I don't want a rough transcript with every UML left in. I want clean sentences that still sound like me, with nothing added and nothing removed. Names, numbers and dates matter the most, because those are the things I will act on later. The third priority is speed, but only in the background I don't mind if a thoughts 15 or 20 seconds to process, as long as the recording itself starts instantly. After that I want related thoughts to be grouped together. If I record for ideas on a morning walk about the same project, I want to see one clear note, not four fragments. And finally the app should tell me the truth about what it's doing. If something failed, show me that it failed and let me retry. If the phone is too hot or low on memory, wait and try again later. I would rather see an honest delay than a wrong result. That's the plan. I'll review it again at the end of the month and decide what to change.",
